    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "can u quickly summarize the actual steps a company has to follow when someone submits a \"right to be forgotten\" request under gdpr? just need the main points for a memo.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When a \"right to be forgotten\" request is received under GDPR, the company must first verify the identity of the requester to ensure they are who they claim to be. Next, the company must assess if any legal basis exists (like contractual necessity or overriding public interest) that prevents them from complying with the request. If the request is valid, the company must erase the personal data in all systems and inform any third parties who previously received that data. Finally, a timely response, usually within one month, detailing the decision and reasoning, must be provided to the individual.",
