    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. what about the data that's backed up or stored in secondary/archived systems though? do we have to go in and manually scrub every single backup tape or something?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Handling backups is one of the trickier parts of the right to erasure. If the data is truly irrecoverable or cannot be deleted from the backup systems using standard technical methods, you may not have to immediately scrub every single tape. However, the general principle requires that when the backup is next cycled or overwritten, the data must be permanently purged. You must document this process clearly to demonstrate compliance to the supervisory authority.",
